WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:10.160
City bus and transit riders got a lifeline&nbsp;
in the latest pandemic related relief bill&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:14.480
New York City's subway system will get&nbsp;
billions, though much less than it asks for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:20.560
Don't think of this as a bailout to the profligate.&nbsp;
The aid begins to correct for an historic inequity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:25.280
The federal government has long been subsidizing&nbsp;
our least efficient systems in rural and small&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:31.680
town America, and neglecting cities. Transit aid&nbsp;in a time of crisis should not reward cities for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:38.160
decades of fiscal mismanagement, but should help&nbsp;them get past COVID and chart a path to stability&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:42.800
New York's is the most used public transit&nbsp;
system in the U.S. and typically does not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:48.459
rely on any federal help to run the system. Now&nbsp;compare it to Oneida in upstate New York. &nbsp;

00:00:48.459 --> 00:00:54.080
Currently the Big Apple has lost most of its subway&nbsp;riders and fares. Congress filling that gap&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.080 --> 00:01:00.400
is necessary and timely, lest cities be robbed&nbsp;of the ability to rebound. Any post-pandemic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:06.320
aid should require that they economize, but when&nbsp;
it comes to transit cities should no longer be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:07.428
disfavored. 

00:01:08.863 --> 00:01:13.920
Do you think big cities should get&nbsp;
more federal transit aid? Let us know in our poll&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:17.520
Also, let us know what other topics&nbsp;
you'd like our scholars to cover&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:24.400
in 60 seconds. And be sure to like and&nbsp;
subscribe for more research and videos from AEI

